Z||000000||Julian||11-12-2000||10:36 PM||||OK people I know we heard this question before but here goes... I need to redo my entire factory sound system in my 1988 Fiero Mera.  I saw some guy here spend a bazillion bucks decking out the car & winning sound shows. (this I don't need).  Here is what I need... am/fm/CD... maybe a sub... amp?? all new speakers. Here is my question.... what is a good system that will work with the factory plug in harnes? And where should I put a sub if I need one? (never came with a sub)???????||||reg||6
Z||000001||Philphine||11-12-2000||10:48 PM||||is the stereo setup the same as a regular fiero?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Julian||11-12-2000||11:03 PM||||yeah the stereo looks like a regular Fiero model....2 speakers on the dash...2 in the sails...no sub on this ...may have been removed. Actually the stereo has a built in 5 band equalizer.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://homepages.go.com/~mera8071/Dcp_0016.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000003||Oreif||11-13-2000||02:18 AM||||Pioneer makes a very nice AM/FM/CD player that fits in the large GM spots. Many places sell an adapter you solder to the aftermarket radio and it plugs into a stock Fiero connector. The sell them for the speaker connectors also.<P>If you want to use a newer GM radio, go to <A HREF="http://www.newellelectronics.com" TARGET=_blank>www.newellelectronics.com</A>   <BR>They sell harness adapters to go from a new GM radio to the older cars. As well as used GM radio's.<P>As for a sub you could buy a stock set-up or if going aftermarket, Bazooka makes a 6" powered sub that fits behind the passenger seat. You can get it with 35W or 80W amps.<BR> Originally I had a Pioneer radio, speakers, and the Bazooka tube in my car. I think total cost was close to $550.00 for everything. Right now I am installing a larger system complete with amps, larger sub, sound processor, and 8 speakers.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 11-13-2000).]||||reg||1
